sdata> -- Issue #63 / ADR-054: REMOVE n[-m] is the renamed program-buffer line
sdata> -- editor command (was DELETE n[-m]). This is its first real end-to-end
sdata> -- REPL integration test -- previously this whole command family
sdata> -- (INSERT/LIST/REMOVE) was only exercised via interpreter_unit_test.adb's
sdata> -- direct Immediate()/Queue() procedure calls, never through an actual
sdata> -- REPL session (the same gap issue #69 closed generally).
sdata> --
sdata> -- Buffer built as [A=1, A=2, A=3, A=4]; REMOVE 2-3 drops the middle two
sdata> -- lines -> [A=1, A=4]; RUN leaves A=4.
sdata> LET A = 1
sdata> LET A = 2
sdata> LET A = 3
sdata> LET A = 4
sdata> REMOVE 2-3
sdata> RUN
RUN complete. 1 records and 1 variables processed.
sdata> PRINT A
sdata> RUN
4.00000
RUN complete. 1 records and 1 variables processed.
sdata> QUIT
